codex
The dependency graph is acyclic and resolves to four internal phases: profile/key foundation; trust and connection in parallel; diagnostics/privacy; then onboarding/accessibility/migration and physical acceptance. I’m attaching three narrow diagrams to their owning contract tasks and a board-only decomposition summary to the epic.
exec
/bin/zsh -lc "task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260715-2hhh7x, name=TASK-260715-2hhh7x_credential-boundaries.puml, content=\"@startuml\\n"'!theme plain'"\\nleft to right direction\\ntitle M4 Profile, Credential, and Extension Boundaries\\n\\nactor User\\n\\npackage \\\"Containing apps\\\" {\\n  [ReluxProxyIOS] as IOS\\n  [ReluxProxyMac] as Mac\\n  [Profile and Key Repository] as Repo\\n}\\n\\ndatabase \\\"App Group Profile Store\\\\nversioned non-secret snapshots\\\\napproved host identities\\\\nopaque Keychain references\\\" as AppGroup\\ndatabase \\\"Data Protection Keychain\\\\nprivate keys and optional passphrases\\\\nminimum shared access group\\\" as Keychain\\ncomponent \\\"NETunnelProviderManager\\\\nschema plus opaque profile reference only\\\" as Manager\\n\\npackage \\\"Packet tunnel extensions\\\" {\\n  [Provider Adapter] as Provider\\n  [ReluxTunnelCore Runtime] as Runtime\\n}\\n\\nnode \\\"User-owned SSH host\\\" as Host\\n\\nUser --> IOS : edit profile / manage keys / approve trust\\nUser --> Mac : edit profile / manage keys / approve trust\\nIOS --> Repo : typed actions\\nMac --> Repo : typed actions\\nRepo --> AppGroup : atomic generation publish\\nRepo --> Keychain : secret CRUD\\nIOS --> Manager : select opaque profile generation\\nMac --> Manager : select opaque profile generation\\nManager --> Provider : start with non-secret reference\\nProvider --> AppGroup : load immutable generation\\nProvider --> Keychain : resolve opaque credential after host approval\\nProvider --> Runtime : compose verified profile and credential\\nRuntime --> Host : verify host key, then authenticate\\nProvider --> IOS : versioned status, trust, and diagnostics evidence\\nProvider --> Mac : versioned status, trust, and diagnostics evidence\\n\\nnote bottom of AppGroup\\n  Forbidden: raw private keys, passphrases,\\n  traffic, DNS queries, and destination data\\nend note\\n\\nnote bottom of Keychain\\n  Secrets never enter providerConfiguration,\\n  logs, diagnostics, or board resources\\nend note\\n\\n@enduml\", type=outcome, description=\"Solution-architecture component view of App Group, Keychain, manager, provider, and SSH trust boundaries\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-31zqvw, name=TASK-260715-31zqvw_mandatory-host-trust-sequence.puml, content=\"@startuml\\n"'!theme plain'"\\ntitle Mandatory Host Trust Before Authentication\\n\\nactor User\\nparticipant \\\"Containing App\\\" as App\\ndatabase \\\"Versioned Profile Store\\\" as Profiles\\nparticipant \\\"Packet Tunnel Provider\\\" as Provider\\nparticipant \\\"Host Identity Policy\\\" as Policy\\ndatabase \\\"Shared Keychain\\\" as Keychain\\nparticipant \\\"User-owned SSH Host\\\" as Host\\n\\nUser -> App : Connect selected profile\\nApp -> Provider : Start(profileID, generation)\\nProvider -> Profiles : Load immutable non-secret snapshot\\nProvider -> Host : Open transport and receive server host key\\nProvider -> Policy : Evaluate canonical host and key evidence\\n\\nalt First use: no approved identity\\n  Policy --> Provider : trustRequired(full SHA-256, algorithm, generation)\\n  Provider --> App : Versioned bounded trust evidence\\n  Provider -> Provider : Stop safely before credential lookup\\n  App -> User : Show complete fingerprint and explicit actions\\n  alt User explicitly trusts\\n    User -> App : Approve reviewed identity\\n    App -> Profiles : Atomically publish generation + 1\\n    User -> App : Explicit retry\\n    App -> Provider : Start(new generation)\\n  else User cancels\\n    User -> App : Cancel\\n    App -> App : Keep profile untrusted and disconnected\\n  end\\nelse Approved identity matches\\n  Policy --> Provider : approved(identity generation)\\n  Provider -> Keychain : Resolve opaque key/passphrase reference\\n  Keychain --> Provider : Bounded secret material\\n  Provider -> Host : Public-key authentication\\n  Host --> Provider : Authenticated session or typed rejection\\nelse Changed, revoked, or lane-inconsistent identity\\n  Policy --> Provider : terminal identity mismatch\\n  Provider --> App : High-severity changed-key evidence\\n  Provider -> Provider : Stop before Keychain and authentication\\n  App -> User : Inspect old/new fingerprints; replace or cancel\\nend\\n\\nnote over Provider,Keychain\\n  The extension never waits indefinitely for foreground UI.\\n  Approval is durable; retry is a fresh explicit generation.\\nend note\\n\\n@enduml\", type=outcome, description=\"Solution-architecture sequence for first use, approved identity, changed key, and auth ordering\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-2a1cp7, name=TASK-260715-2a1cp7_connection-state-contract.puml, content=\"@startuml\\n"'!theme plain'"\\nleft to right direction\\nhide empty description\\ntitle User-visible VPN Connection State Contract\\n\\nstate \\\"Disconnected\\\" as Disconnected\\nstate \\\"Connecting\\\" as Connecting\\nstate \\\"Connected / Full\\\" as Full\\nstate \\\"Connected / Degraded\\\" as Degraded\\nstate \\\"Reasserting\\\" as Reasserting\\nstate \\\"Disconnecting\\\" as Disconnecting\\nstate \\\"Failed\\\" as Failed\\n\\n[*] --> Disconnected\\n\\nDisconnected --> Connecting : explicit connect\\\\neligible profile + disclosure\\nConnecting --> Full : session connected\\\\ncurrent generation has TCP + safe DNS + UDP\\nConnecting --> Degraded : session connected\\\\ncurrent generation has TCP + safe DNS, no UDP\\nConnecting --> Failed : mandatory startup failure\\nConnecting --> Disconnecting : explicit stop\\n\\nFull --> Degraded : relay/UDP lost\\\\nbase TCP + safe DNS remain\\nDegraded --> Full : validated relay generation restored\\n\\nFull --> Reasserting : path/transport/settings recovery\\nDegraded --> Reasserting : mandatory base recovery begins\\nReasserting --> Full : current generation fully restored\\nReasserting --> Degraded : current generation safely degraded\\nReasserting --> Failed : bounded recovery ends unsafely\\n\\nFull --> Disconnecting : explicit stop\\nDegraded --> Disconnecting : explicit stop\\nReasserting --> Disconnecting : explicit stop\\nFailed --> Connecting : explicit retry\\nFailed --> Disconnected : acknowledge / clear failed attempt\\nDisconnecting --> Disconnected : system confirms stop\\n\\nnote top of Full\\n  Full requires a fresh provider capability snapshot.\\n  Cached app state cannot create this state.\\nend note\\n\\nnote bottom of Degraded\\n  Still connected: eligible TCP and leak-safe DNS continue.\\n  General UDP is unavailable and must be named explicitly.\\nend note\\n\\nnote bottom of Failed\\n  Reserved for a requirement without which\\n  safe forwarding cannot continue.\\nend note\\n\\n@enduml\", type=outcome, description=\"Solution-architecture state view for disconnected through full, degraded, reasserting, failed, and stop\")'" in /Users/iv/Developer/relux-proxy
