all task-owned temporary artifacts. 4. The pipeline never performs network I/O or analytics and does not retain a hidden copy after platform handoff. 5. Unit/integration/golden/property tests verify manifest parity, category selection, redaction idempotence, limits, cleanup, reproducibility, and successful inspection on both platforms.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-2bgp7x","TASK-260715-1m2xet","TASK-260715-2o2oq0"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-3c7g17","TASK-260715-o07tjd"],"checklist":[{"text":"Deliver the stated scope while preserving every explicit non-scope boundary","done":false},{"text":"Verify every acceptance criterion with the specified automated or manual evidence","done":false},{"text":"Attach a TASK-260715-2f44rv-scoped redacted outcome with commands artifacts and residual risks","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T02:38:02Z","description":"Implement a user-initiated pipeline that snapshots approved diagnostic categories, reapplies the documented redaction pass, creates a human-readable manifest, enforces size limits, and cleans protected temporary artifacts on success, cancellation, expiration, or failure.","id":"TASK-260715-2f44rv","isBlocked":true,"name":"implement-support-export-redaction-and-manifest-pipeline","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-3tds7d","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: explicit request, selected categories, immutable input snapshot, defense-in-depth redaction, deterministic JSON/text formats, schema/build/device/OS/source metadata allowed by contract, category manifest, file names, archive generation, byte/count limits, progress/cancellation, Data Protection/temp permissions, collision handling, cleanup, export audit event, and tests. Out of scope: automatic upload, support ticket creation, packet capture, destination/DNS data, production secrets, UI, and retention after the user moves the file.","status":"backlog","title":"Implement the support-export redaction and manifest pipeli